    [BugFix][Model] Backport SWA bounded replay to vLLM 0.30 (#18322)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    Backport the opt-in SWA bounded replay admission protocol to vLLM 0.30.0
    so the Ascend DeepSeek V4.1 worker can rebuild its SWA window after a
    local prefix-cache hit without replacing installed vLLM source files or
    compiled operators.
    
    Adds replay configuration and CLI flags, request payload boundaries,
    scheduler rewind and allocation handling, and private SWA cache
    behavior. Native replay implementations are detected and retained. KV
    connectors are rejected for the legacy replay path. Includes regression
    tests, a real-weight response comparison probe, and validation
    instructions.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    Yes. On the legacy vLLM 0.30.0 path, users can opt in with
    `--enable-prefix-caching --swa-bounded-replay` and explicitly disable
    replay with `--no-swa-bounded-replay`. The feature defaults to disabled.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - Passed Python AST syntax validation for all 9 changed Python files.
    - Passed `git diff --check`.
    - Dynamic dataclass serialization/idempotence and classmethod binding
    smoke checks passed for the CI fix.
    - CI type-check fix at `50f82fe7e6`: Ruff 0.14.0 check and format passed
    for the changed file; targeted mypy with `--follow-imports skip
    --check-untyped-defs --python-version 3.10 --ignore-missing-imports`
    passed locally. GitHub pre-commit (including full mypy checks) and Docs
    link check passed for this commit; the two CPU unit-test jobs are still
